# omaishort

Story → short-video engine, not a TikTok clone. Quality bar: `.cursor/rules/quality.mdc`.

Three kinds, one pipeline: `kind=drama` (short story, bible faces, motion), `kind=news` / `kind=knowledge` (editorial **ảnh ghép**, narrator VO). Legacy `brief` aliases to `news`.

- Do not emit one image per sentence. A scene has `duration_sec` plus 1–3 `shots` on one `still_id`.
- Drama is the **short-story** kind: bible faces, close-up beat lenses, I2V when keyed. **Default:** user still prompts who/what; tell it in humiliation → reveal → karma **shape**. **Custom:** prompt is another story from scratch (not that shape). Always one continuous five-beat short.
- News/knowledge are **ảnh ghép** (editorial still collage + Ken Burns), not character cinema. Bible is narrator-only. Scene `characters` is empty. `use_face_ref=false`. Stills prefer **article photos** (`source_url` src) on early beats, then **per-beat** Wikimedia/Openverse terms, then generated editorial. Knowledge **topic** pastes write VO first (`script.json`): in-process ChatGPT web (`providers/chatgpt_web.py`, profile in `DATA_DIR/chatgpt-web`, headed `--chatgpt-login` once then headless, **one conversation per calendar day**) then OpenAI-compatible HTTP, else wiki. Do not clone ChatGPT-Web2API, chatgpt-pro-web, or HyperFrames. Do not scrape Gemini/Midjourney UIs; image adapters are HTTP (Pollinations, Gemini API, OpenAI). Do not use Pexels.
- Beats: hook / conflict / rising_action / twist / ending. News maps those keys to headline / obstacle / unfold / turn / outcome. Knowledge maps them to claim / proof / context / misconception / remember. `normalize_storyboard` applies beat lenses (do not leave random hold/zoom cycles).
- Providers are protocols. Planner never imports a vendor SDK. Image: Pollinations (turbo/kontext) → Gemini API (if keyed) → OpenAI → placeholder. Comfy stub when a photo is not required. Video: HF Spaces (needs `HF_TOKEN`) → WaveSpeed Wan HTTP (if keyed) → Pollinations Wan or Seedance (pollen) → Comfy stub → Ken Burns. Seedance is closed HTTP (Ark/BytePlus/pollen), not a cloned “free” GitHub Space. WaveSpeed is the same HTTP submit/poll shape — do not clone ginigen Spaces that wrap it.
- Ken Burns: 2160×3840 working frame, cosine ease, 1080×1920 out. Editorial stills letterbox wide photos and skip close_up punch-ins. I2V: **drama only**, one clip per scene; news/knowledge stay Ken Burns. Motion prompt is camera + action only.
- Stages: analyze → plan → refs → stills → tts → captions → render. After TTS, rescale times to real audio.
- Remotion only reads `timeline.json`. `elements[].type` is `video` only for real I2V clips.

Schema: `packages/schema/omaishort_schema/models.py`. Product: `docs/REQUIREMENTS.md`. Sources: `docs/RESEARCH.md`.
